WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }
::cue(c.colora8c7fa) { color: #a8c7fa; }
::cue(c.credits) { color: #a8c7fa; font-size: 78%; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Premium</c></b>
Keep the project alive: <c.colora8c7fa>ko-fi.com/not6ip</c>

2
00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:14.630
Inherited will...

3
00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:17.540
the tides of time,
and humanity's dreams...

4
00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:20.370
They cannot be stopped.

5
00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:23.480
As long as people seek freedom,

6
00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:26.110
these things will never cease to be.

7
00:01:50.260 --> 00:01:54.090
<b>I Love My Country</b>

8
00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:59.170
So it hasn't rained for three years.
What of it?

9
00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:07.450
I have faith in His Majesty, 
as does most of the country.

10
00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:11.520
So many times...

11
00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:13.550
So many times I tried to stop them.

12
00:02:15.670 --> 00:02:18.470
But they never listened to me.

13
00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:20.530
The rebellion won't stop.

14
00:02:21.350 --> 00:02:25.320
But they've about reached their limit.

15
00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:29.000
They intend to settle things once 
and for all with their next attack.

16
00:02:29.490 --> 00:02:32.150
Their backs are to the wall...

17
00:02:36.330 --> 00:02:37.880
They're prepared to die!

18
00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:46.280
Please, Vivi-chan ! 
You have to stop those fools!

19
00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:56.780
<b>Katorea</b>

20
00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:05.490
– Where's our leader?
– Inside.

21
00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:24.890
Uncle Toto, rest assured...

22
00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:26.630
Vivi-chan...

23
00:03:28.490 --> 00:03:31.440
...we will stop the rebellion.

24
00:03:41.310 --> 00:03:42.740
Thank you!

25
00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:03.460
So long, Vivi-chan.
This is goodbye for now.

26
00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:07.370
When the city is up and running, 
come and visit sometime.

27
00:04:07.370 --> 00:04:09.430
I will, Uncle Toto!

28
00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:14.440
We'll build an awesome city that'll 
increase this country's greenery!

29
00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:21.360
Bye, Vivi! 
Grow up to be a great princess!

30
00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:23.450
Yeah!

31
00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:36.710
Koza!

32
00:04:37.470 --> 00:04:39.610
I've contacted everyone in the other towns.

33
00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:49.240
This is it. 
The time to strike has come.

34
00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:53.430
Yes. We don't have nearly
enough weapons, though.

35
00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:57.020
Even so, it's now or never.

36
00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:01.520
The only ones who can
protect this country...

37
00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:05.530
are us!

38
00:05:07.850 --> 00:05:09.320
I won't let you have her!

39
00:05:09.320 --> 00:05:11.370
Protect her to the death, Sand-Sand Clan!

40
00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:26.880
Some bodyguards, huh?

41
00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:28.510
There are more of 'em?!

42
00:05:30.010 --> 00:05:31.720
Ow! Ow! Ow!

43
00:05:32.440 --> 00:05:33.390
Damn! She got away!

44
00:05:35.820 --> 00:05:38.230
The ruins are that way! Catch her!

45
00:05:41.190 --> 00:05:42.440
Don't let 'em go!

46
00:05:44.620 --> 00:05:45.320
Move!

47
00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:50.990
What in the world?!

48
00:05:57.680 --> 00:06:01.960
Hey! What happened to you?!
What happened here?!

49
00:06:02.940 --> 00:06:06.310
Some bad guys... were after Vivi...

50
00:06:06.310 --> 00:06:07.380
What?!

51
00:06:08.490 --> 00:06:10.580
Grown-ups with blades...

52
00:06:10.580 --> 00:06:12.450
They just went into the ruins!

53
00:06:12.450 --> 00:06:14.350
Koza chased after 'em too!

54
00:06:14.820 --> 00:06:16.020
What?!

55
00:06:19.990 --> 00:06:26.200
– Oh, Princess! 
– Where are you, Princess?

56
00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:28.040
Where the hell are you hiding?

57
00:06:28.040 --> 00:06:30.680
Find her! Find her!
Don't let her get away!

58
00:06:30.680 --> 00:06:34.330
Princess Vivi! Come on out!

59
00:06:42.600 --> 00:06:44.630
Oh, there you are!

60
00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:49.130
Please, be a good girl 
and get kidnapped already.

61
00:06:51.920 --> 00:06:53.540
Not so fast!

62
00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:56.010
Leader!

63
00:06:57.690 --> 00:06:59.170
You alright, Vivi?!

64
00:07:00.630 --> 00:07:02.020
Ow... Ouch!

65
00:07:02.810 --> 00:07:05.900
Don't underestimate 
the Sand-Sand Clan, villain!

66
00:07:06.390 --> 00:07:08.400
Leave this city at once!

67
00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:13.010
Look here, boy. 
Just shut it and give up the princess.

68
00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:17.600
You should know better 
than to piss off grown-ups.

69
00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:20.210
A blade! Let's run away, Leader!

70
00:07:21.610 --> 00:07:24.290
– That doesn't scare me!
– Huh?!

71
00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:32.180
Protect her to the death, Sand-Sand Clan!

72
00:07:33.210 --> 00:07:35.270
Leader! Don't do this!

73
00:07:35.270 --> 00:07:37.720
You wanna fight, huh?

74
00:08:12.930 --> 00:08:13.630
Leader!

75
00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:18.640
That punk knocked out the boss!

76
00:08:19.390 --> 00:08:22.850
What the hell?! 
Let's put the hurt on 'im!

77
00:08:25.280 --> 00:08:27.100
Alright! C'mere!

78
00:08:27.100 --> 00:08:28.690
Hey, you!

79
00:08:30.840 --> 00:08:32.690
You cretins!

80
00:08:33.190 --> 00:08:35.200
Daddy! Igaram!

81
00:08:35.770 --> 00:08:37.930
Your Highness! Are you all right?!

82
00:08:37.110 --> 00:08:37.930
Curse you!

83
00:08:37.930 --> 00:08:41.160
Thought you could
kidnap my daughter, did you?!

84
00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:45.710
You lousy vagabonds!
Take this! And this! And this!

85
00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:47.540
These appear to be their friends.

86
00:08:48.980 --> 00:08:52.590
Chaka! Pell! 
What are you doing here?

87
00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:56.420
Why? We could ask you 
the same thing.

88
00:08:56.420 --> 00:09:00.200
What is the king doing in a place
like this, away from the palace?

89
00:09:00.740 --> 00:09:03.190
You should refrain 
from acting so recklessly.

90
00:09:05.120 --> 00:09:06.560
Igaram! Koza's hurt!

91
00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:09.840
Yes! A doctor should tend to him immediately!

92
00:09:09.840 --> 00:09:12.280
The Sand-Sand Clan members
atop the hill, too!

93
00:09:12.280 --> 00:09:14.120
Chaka! Pell! 
Make arrangements at once!

94
00:09:14.120 --> 00:09:14.530
Yes, sir!

95
00:09:15.960 --> 00:09:18.060
What brave children!

96
00:09:24.400 --> 00:09:28.460
What is the matter, Vivi? 
Why so glum?

97
00:09:29.130 --> 00:09:31.970
I was so scared...

98
00:09:33.260 --> 00:09:34.920
Yeah, I was scared too.

99
00:09:35.560 --> 00:09:37.930
They even had blades on them...

100
00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:39.840
That's not it!

101
00:09:41.260 --> 00:09:46.350
You told them to protect me 
to the death, Leader...

102
00:09:46.350 --> 00:09:48.890
Protect her to the death, Sand-Sand Clan!

103
00:09:53.450 --> 00:09:57.000
Don't talk about dying, Leader...

104
00:09:59.310 --> 00:10:03.590
Oh, more than anything,
she was afraid of losing her friends.

105
00:10:14.130 --> 00:10:17.680
Vivi may be young, 
but she is also a princess, Koza.

106
00:10:18.260 --> 00:10:21.840
The enormity of your deed today 
will not go unnoticed.

107
00:10:21.840 --> 00:10:24.220
You have my gratitude. Thank you.

108
00:10:25.420 --> 00:10:28.640
Vivi's a friend. It was only natural.

109
00:10:29.550 --> 00:10:30.600
Indeed.

110
00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:34.990
I can tell the next generation 
of Arabasta will be in good hands.

111
00:10:34.990 --> 00:10:36.820
Do you like this country?

112
00:10:36.820 --> 00:10:39.610
Yeah! It's my homeland!

113
00:10:39.610 --> 00:10:41.350
I feel the same!

114
00:10:43.570 --> 00:10:45.030
Though I...

115
00:10:47.930 --> 00:10:50.440
I am also a bit concerned.

116
00:10:50.440 --> 00:10:51.540
How so?

117
00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:58.260
Your high position ceaselessly asks 
that you make difficult decisions.

118
00:10:58.260 --> 00:11:01.590
Vivi-sama is too kindhearted for that.

119
00:11:01.590 --> 00:11:03.450
Igaram.

120
00:11:03.450 --> 00:11:04.270
Yes, sire?

121
00:11:05.700 --> 00:11:09.740
This is fine. Arabasta is
fine just as it is now.

122
00:11:15.330 --> 00:11:20.580
Allow me to accompany you,
for as long as I live!

123
00:11:21.550 --> 00:11:22.610
Yuba?

124
00:11:22.610 --> 00:11:27.040
Yeah! Your dad talked
to my dad about it!

125
00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:28.910
Uncle Toto?

126
00:11:28.910 --> 00:11:33.880
He was asked to break new ground
at the uninhabited Yuba Oasis.

127
00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:35.340
<b>Yuba</b>

128
00:11:36.190 --> 00:11:39.820
That area's like 
the crossroads of Arabasta,

129
00:11:39.820 --> 00:11:43.080
where every traveler 
and merchant pass through!

130
00:11:42.220 --> 00:11:44.930
<b>Yuba</b>

131
00:11:43.180 --> 00:11:43.390
<b>Yubaba</b>

132
00:11:43.650 --> 00:11:46.300
Just wait till it's built 
and becomes a city!

133
00:11:44.270 --> 00:11:44.430
<b>Yubaba</b>

134
00:11:44.930 --> 00:11:45.180
<b>Yubaubaba</b>

135
00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:47.940
<b>Yuba</b>

136
00:11:46.190 --> 00:11:46.390
<b>Yubaubaa</b>

137
00:11:46.300 --> 00:11:49.320
It'll make so many citizens happy!

138
00:11:47.940 --> 00:11:51.070
<b>Yuba</b>

139
00:11:49.310 --> 00:11:49.560
<b>Yuba uba</b>

140
00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:49.690
<b>Yubaa</b>

141
00:11:49.900 --> 00:11:50.190
<b>Yubaubaa</b>

142
00:11:51.070 --> 00:11:52.440
<b>Yuba</b>

143
00:11:52.800 --> 00:11:53.770
Awesome, huh?!

144
00:11:54.740 --> 00:11:58.150
And my dad was asked
to be its representative!

145
00:11:58.150 --> 00:11:59.840
Are you going too, Leader?

146
00:11:59.840 --> 00:12:00.990
Of course!

147
00:12:01.380 --> 00:12:03.780
My dad wants me to stay here...

148
00:12:04.430 --> 00:12:08.210
I'm sure starting a city isn't easy...

149
00:12:08.210 --> 00:12:09.350
but I'm gonna do it!

150
00:12:09.350 --> 00:12:11.750
I'm gonna build a new city
with my own two hands!

151
00:12:12.440 --> 00:12:15.030
Yuba's exactly what 
this country needs!

152
00:12:23.470 --> 00:12:25.360
Make us proud, Toto.

153
00:12:25.360 --> 00:12:29.890
Yes, Your Majesty!
We will build a wonderful city!

154
00:12:30.500 --> 00:12:33.390
So long, Vivi-chan.
This is goodbye for now.

155
00:12:33.390 --> 00:12:37.110
When the city is up and running,
come and visit sometime.

156
00:12:37.610 --> 00:12:39.400
I will, Uncle Toto!

157
00:12:40.130 --> 00:12:44.200
We'll build an awesome city that'll 
increase this country's greenery!

158
00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:46.160
Time to go!

159
00:12:46.160 --> 00:12:50.650
Bye, Vivi! Grow up to be a great princess!

160
00:12:51.660 --> 00:12:52.630
Yeah!

161
00:12:54.630 --> 00:12:57.030
Koza! You're too casual with her!

162
00:12:57.030 --> 00:12:57.890
Ow!

163
00:12:59.570 --> 00:13:01.670
Koza is right.

164
00:13:02.790 --> 00:13:06.070
Yuba will surely increase 
this country's greenery.

165
00:13:11.450 --> 00:13:15.590
Excellent work today, my good men!

166
00:13:16.270 --> 00:13:21.480
So let's hit the hay for now and 
regain our strength for tomorrow!

167
00:13:21.480 --> 00:13:22.990
Nighty-night!

168
00:13:25.100 --> 00:13:26.880
You've been sleeping all day!

169
00:13:27.400 --> 00:13:28.960
Why, you...

170
00:13:28.960 --> 00:13:32.080
I don't have the endurance 
of you monsters!

171
00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:35.260
Now you've done it!

172
00:13:36.020 --> 00:13:39.840
Besides, you win today's
laziness award, Blue Nose!

173
00:13:39.840 --> 00:13:41.880
I'm not built for hot weather!

174
00:13:41.880 --> 00:13:43.380
Sanji-san. That's my–

175
00:13:43.380 --> 00:13:46.760
Yes. I thought you might have a
hard time sleeping alone tonight.

176
00:13:47.840 --> 00:13:50.800
And just what are you up to, mister?

177
00:13:50.800 --> 00:13:52.640
Oh, that took some nerve.

178
00:13:52.640 --> 00:13:55.770
Which one of you 
is spoiling for a fight?!

179
00:13:55.770 --> 00:13:58.520
Do you guys not understand
the point of shut-eye?!

180
00:13:59.580 --> 00:14:01.150
That's it! You're in trouble now!

181
00:14:12.140 --> 00:14:17.660
Hey, old guy. There's still no water. 
My throat's bone-dry...

182
00:14:17.660 --> 00:14:20.580
How do you even live here? 
This is bad.

183
00:14:20.580 --> 00:14:24.700
There'll be water.
The Yuba Oasis yet lives.

184
00:14:24.700 --> 00:14:27.460
Yuba, you see, can't be beaten 
by some lousy sand!

185
00:14:27.460 --> 00:14:29.750
I'll dig it back up
as many times as it takes!

186
00:14:29.750 --> 00:14:34.560
The king himself entrusted me 
with this very important land.

187
00:14:37.390 --> 00:14:39.340
Oh, okay! If so, let's dig!

188
00:14:40.360 --> 00:14:44.360
Oh! Wait! Stop!
Don't refill the hole I just dug!

189
00:14:45.530 --> 00:14:48.190
Are you trying to fill the holes?!

190
00:14:48.750 --> 00:14:50.950
No, I'm digging.

191
00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:55.030
No! The sand you're digging up is landing in the hole I just dug,

192
00:14:55.030 --> 00:14:58.910
so I'm trying to say that all my
hard work will be for nothing!

193
00:14:59.500 --> 00:15:00.390
Oh.

194
00:15:01.190 --> 00:15:03.420
Oh! So it's a mystery hole!

195
00:15:05.260 --> 00:15:06.330
Not even close!

196
00:15:18.840 --> 00:15:21.270
Actually, the sand isn't 
flying this way now.

197
00:15:24.080 --> 00:15:26.230
All this, in such a short time?!

198
00:15:27.420 --> 00:15:29.690
Despite being tired 
from a long journey...

199
00:15:39.430 --> 00:15:41.750
May you rest well tonight.

200
00:15:43.850 --> 00:15:44.860
Meat...

201
00:15:47.160 --> 00:15:48.230
Pleasant dreams.

202
00:15:48.930 --> 00:15:54.640
<b>Casino
Rain Dinners</b>

203
00:15:50.450 --> 00:15:53.160
Nobody's clowning here!

204
00:15:54.960 --> 00:15:57.600
Just how long are you
going to make us wait?!

205
00:15:57.600 --> 00:15:59.420
The least you could do
 is offer me an octopar!

206
00:15:59.420 --> 00:16:03.600
Don't make me dance! I'm a swan!
Don't make me spin around!

207
00:16:06.010 --> 00:16:08.770
Mr. 2, please wait quietly.

208
00:16:09.410 --> 00:16:10.860
Seriously! You imbecile! Imba! Imb!

209
00:16:10.860 --> 00:16:12.900
You make my back hurt!

210
00:16:10.860 --> 00:16:13.360
You too, Miss Merry Christmas.

211
00:16:14.690 --> 00:16:17.330
Seems it's too tall an order 
to have you get along.

212
00:16:17.700 --> 00:16:20.710
That won't be necessary anyway.

213
00:16:21.830 --> 00:16:23.790
Miss All Sunday...

214
00:16:23.790 --> 00:16:27.780
I want to thank you all for gathering here—

215
00:16:27.780 --> 00:16:31.050
here, where the people 
gamble big to win big:

216
00:16:31.050 --> 00:16:33.510
the City of Dreams, Rainbase!

217
00:16:33.510 --> 00:16:38.470
Welcome to Rain Dinners,
the city's largest casino!

218
00:16:38.470 --> 00:16:43.440
Could you skip the formalities and
cut to the chase, Miss All Sunday?

219
00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:46.120
Very well. 
I'll get right to the point.

220
00:16:46.120 --> 00:16:50.400
Yeah! Get started! Started! 
Start! Sta! Sta! St! St! S!

221
00:16:50.400 --> 00:16:51.860
But before we begin,

222
00:16:51.860 --> 00:16:56.910
allow me to introduce our company's boss, whose face you've never seen.

223
00:16:57.620 --> 00:17:03.020
Up until now, I've worked as his 
proxy to dole out assignments,

224
00:17:03.020 --> 00:17:05.350
but there is no longer any need for that.

225
00:17:05.350 --> 00:17:06.630
I take it you understand.

226
00:17:07.330 --> 00:17:09.450
At last, the time has come...

227
00:17:10.780 --> 00:17:13.380
for Operation Utopia.

228
00:17:15.760 --> 00:17:17.180
Crocodile?!

229
00:17:18.130 --> 00:17:22.140
This will be Baroque Works' 
ultimate operation.

230
00:17:22.640 --> 00:17:27.100
It would seem you know who he is...
well, outwardly, that is.

231
00:17:27.100 --> 00:17:30.680
Of course we do! But one of the 
Seven Warlords of the Sea?!

232
00:17:30.680 --> 00:17:33.610
We really got ourselves 
a big shot here!

233
00:17:34.130 --> 00:17:38.320
All this time, we've been 
kissing up to a pirate?!

234
00:17:38.320 --> 00:17:40.740
You're our boss?

235
00:17:43.320 --> 00:17:44.200
Dissatisfied?

236
00:17:47.210 --> 00:17:49.210
Not exactly dissatisfied,

237
00:17:49.210 --> 00:17:52.950
but the Seven Warlords 
are government-sanctioned pirates.

238
00:17:52.950 --> 00:17:54.960
Why even run 
this kind of outfit?

239
00:17:57.280 --> 00:18:01.100
What I want is neither money nor status.

240
00:18:01.830 --> 00:18:03.150
I want military might.

241
00:18:03.150 --> 00:18:04.440
Military might?

242
00:18:06.100 --> 00:18:08.540
Allow me to explain in good order...

243
00:18:15.460 --> 00:18:17.790
my true objective...

244
00:18:17.790 --> 00:18:22.230
and the entire breakdown of
Baroque Works' ultimate operation.

245
00:18:39.620 --> 00:18:43.220
Something like that really
exists in this country?

246
00:18:43.220 --> 00:18:46.050
And we'll steal the entire country
 along with it?

247
00:18:46.050 --> 00:18:48.230
I've got chills running through me!

248
00:18:48.230 --> 00:18:54.190
To clarify, each task we carried out 
was all part of your grand plan?

249
00:18:54.190 --> 00:18:56.360
That's exactly right.

250
00:18:56.360 --> 00:18:58.440
Since Baroque Works was founded,

251
00:18:58.440 --> 00:19:03.840
each job you carried out brought 
this operation ever closer to fruition.

252
00:19:03.840 --> 00:19:07.660
And those letters are your final orders.

253
00:19:07.660 --> 00:19:11.730
At long last, the Kingdom 
of Arabasta will disappear!

254
00:19:13.670 --> 00:19:17.330
When you have each fulfilled your mission,

255
00:19:18.040 --> 00:19:20.720
the Kingdom of Arabasta will self-implode.

256
00:19:21.890 --> 00:19:25.390
And, left with no other choice,
the Rebel and Royal Armies...

257
00:19:26.300 --> 00:19:30.350
will tragically fall into
Baroque Works' hands.

258
00:19:30.920 --> 00:19:35.820
In a single night, 
this land will truly become our utopia.

259
00:19:36.600 --> 00:19:42.090
Operation Utopia is Baroque Works'
last and greatest operation.

260
00:19:42.770 --> 00:19:44.780
Failure is not an option.

261
00:19:45.640 --> 00:19:47.580
We begin at noon tomorrow.

262
00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:49.140
Understood!

263
00:19:49.140 --> 00:19:50.750
I wish you luck.

264
00:19:56.840 --> 00:20:01.670
I must ask that you hold off 
on this so-called Operation Utopia.

265
00:20:05.090 --> 00:20:08.600
Mr. 3. How did you get 
into this secret underground room?

266
00:20:08.600 --> 00:20:12.440
Mr. 3! Just what rock did you 
crawl out from under?!

267
00:20:12.440 --> 00:20:14.770
I'll make good on my orders 
and take you out!

268
00:20:15.220 --> 00:20:17.900
Wait, Mr. 2.

269
00:20:18.380 --> 00:20:21.360
"Crawl out from under"? How impolite.

270
00:20:21.360 --> 00:20:26.790
Since the Spiders Cafe, 
I never strayed from your side.

271
00:20:26.790 --> 00:20:29.950
I even took a ride on Bunchi's car.

272
00:20:29.950 --> 00:20:32.430
Nice to meet you, Boss.

273
00:20:32.430 --> 00:20:36.920
I've come here to humbly ask 
for another chance.

274
00:20:37.540 --> 00:20:41.940
After I failed to accomplish 
my given task, Mr. 2,

275
00:20:41.940 --> 00:20:45.440
it was only natural that you'd be 
swiftly dispatched to end my life.

276
00:20:45.440 --> 00:20:48.760
So I slightly adjusted course 
and headed for the Spiders Cafe,

277
00:20:48.760 --> 00:20:51.930
where we agents are stationed.

278
00:20:51.930 --> 00:20:56.400
Failed to accomplish your task?
What are you talking about?

279
00:20:57.780 --> 00:21:03.320
You know. H-How I let the 
Straw Hats and Princess Vivi escape–

280
00:21:06.560 --> 00:21:09.200
"Escape," you say?!

281
00:21:09.960 --> 00:21:12.170
Then you're telling me 
they're still alive?!

282
00:21:13.400 --> 00:21:15.810
What was it you said 
over the transponder snail?

283
00:21:16.280 --> 00:21:22.460
Did you not tell me you personally took care of the pirates and Vivi?!

284
00:21:22.460 --> 00:21:25.980
Transponder snail?
Wh-What do you mean?

285
00:21:25.980 --> 00:21:30.640
I never used a transponder snail
while on Little Garden.

286
00:21:30.640 --> 00:21:31.830
What?!

287
00:21:33.790 --> 00:21:36.380
Heya, you've reached 
Restaurant de Merde.

288
00:21:36.380 --> 00:21:38.400
Making a reservation?

289
00:21:42.580 --> 00:21:44.430
This isn't good.

290
00:21:44.430 --> 00:21:48.240
So that's why the Unluckies 
never returned from the island.

291
00:21:49.690 --> 00:21:52.560
But, I'm sure you at least rid us 
of a pirate or two?

292
00:21:52.560 --> 00:21:54.450
N-No, actually...

293
00:21:55.710 --> 00:21:58.700
Y-You see, our intelligence report 
was incomplete!

294
00:21:58.700 --> 00:22:01.740
She actually had four pirate escorts,

295
00:22:01.740 --> 00:22:04.420
and there... there was 
also a long-nosed man, and–

296
00:22:04.420 --> 00:22:06.170
Damn you!

297
00:22:06.840 --> 00:22:11.250
Zero-chan ! Come on,
he's obviously just clowning around.

298
00:22:11.250 --> 00:22:12.760
None of it makes any sense!

299
00:22:21.060 --> 00:22:24.110
I... I met them!

300
00:22:24.620 --> 00:22:27.610
I ran into these guys on my way here!

301
00:22:28.040 --> 00:22:28.570
What?!

302
00:22:29.660 --> 00:22:32.550
Him! Him!

303
00:22:32.550 --> 00:22:33.980
Her!

304
00:22:33.980 --> 00:22:35.480
Him!

305
00:22:35.480 --> 00:22:37.180
And him, right?!

306
00:22:37.680 --> 00:22:38.410
And...

307
00:22:39.410 --> 00:22:42.650
this is Miss Wednesday,
who is this kingdom's Princess Vivi!

308
00:22:42.650 --> 00:22:45.920
Meaning they were actually our enemy?!

309
00:22:46.540 --> 00:22:50.080
Yes. They know my identity.

310
00:22:50.080 --> 00:22:53.390
They will interfere 
with the operation if left alone.

311
00:22:56.330 --> 00:22:58.050
And Mr. 3.

312
00:22:58.560 --> 00:23:04.210
It's as you say; there is one 
more person, including an animal.

313
00:23:05.100 --> 00:23:07.400
Setting the pet aside,

314
00:23:07.400 --> 00:23:13.740
it's safe to assume Vivi and the other four... are already here in Arabasta.

315
00:23:14.250 --> 00:23:17.910
Mr. 2, photograph those faces 
your memory feature recorded.

316
00:23:17.910 --> 00:23:19.820
B-But, Boss!

317
00:23:19.820 --> 00:23:23.290
I swear that I will take care of 
that crew and Vivi with my own two–

318
00:23:23.290 --> 00:23:25.320
Quiet, you damn fool!

319
00:23:27.010 --> 00:23:28.550
Mr. 3...

320
00:23:29.660 --> 00:23:31.380
Mr. 3!

321
00:23:32.360 --> 00:23:36.140
Do you know why 
I gave you your rank?!

322
00:23:37.840 --> 00:23:44.220
In terms of fighting skill alone,
even Mr. 4 outclasses you, Mr. 3!

323
00:23:44.220 --> 00:23:45.820
It was due to that...

324
00:23:45.820 --> 00:23:49.590
underhanded, contemptible tenacity with which you carry out your tasks!

325
00:23:51.600 --> 00:23:53.610
You've really let me down!

326
00:23:53.610 --> 00:23:55.630
Wh-What is that?!

327
00:23:55.630 --> 00:23:57.580
H-He's drying up!

328
00:23:59.660 --> 00:24:01.170
W-Water...

329
00:24:02.760 --> 00:24:04.300
Water...

330
00:24:04.300 --> 00:24:06.020
Have all the water you want.

331
00:24:18.990 --> 00:24:20.750
Time for dinner.

332
00:24:22.660 --> 00:24:26.020
What is this place? Underwater?

333
00:24:28.830 --> 00:24:31.810
I-It's almost like an aquarium...

334
00:24:32.490 --> 00:24:35.550
A b-bananagator!

335
00:24:39.820 --> 00:24:43.160
That sniveling weakling's 
complicated things...

336
00:24:46.390 --> 00:24:49.150
He just doesn't know 
how to stay dead!

337
00:24:51.020 --> 00:24:55.120
Listen, now! 
Take a good look at these five!

338
00:24:55.120 --> 00:24:57.430
They'll stop at nothing to end the rebellion.

339
00:24:57.430 --> 00:25:00.640
If we leave them alone,
they'll eventually come to us!

340
00:25:00.640 --> 00:25:02.700
But, Zero-chan.

341
00:25:02.700 --> 00:25:04.530
Even if she is the princess,

342
00:25:04.530 --> 00:25:08.110
do you really think she can stop
the rebellion at this point?

343
00:25:09.070 --> 00:25:10.980
Unfortunately, our
 intel tells us that...

344
00:25:10.980 --> 00:25:17.450
the rebel leader Koza and Princess 
Nefertari Vivi are longtime friends.

345
00:25:18.660 --> 00:25:20.770
It's a swell of 700,000.

346
00:25:20.770 --> 00:25:23.200
Even if it can't be easily stopped,

347
00:25:23.200 --> 00:25:27.380
she can bring confusion 
to the Rebel Army.

348
00:25:28.120 --> 00:25:31.950
I've already had many
of our billions infiltrate their ranks.

349
00:25:32.620 --> 00:25:35.530
There's been 
no communication from them,

350
00:25:35.530 --> 00:25:39.730
which means they've 
still delayed any direct action.

351
00:25:39.730 --> 00:25:43.100
Whatever the cost, 
Vivi and the Rebel Army...

352
00:25:43.100 --> 00:25:45.660
cannot make contact 
before the operation.

353
00:25:47.980 --> 00:25:49.930
– Miss All Sunday.
– Yes?

354
00:25:50.480 --> 00:25:53.780
Given the circumstances, 
we can use the transponder snails.

355
00:25:53.780 --> 00:25:56.370
Contact the billions in Nanohana.

356
00:25:56.950 --> 00:26:00.070
Give the order to kill on sight.

357
00:26:00.840 --> 00:26:04.200
Do not let Princess Vivi
and the pirates into Katorea!

358
00:26:05.130 --> 00:26:08.200
Vivi and Koza must not 
be allowed to meet!

359
00:26:08.920 --> 00:26:10.360
Yes. Right away.

360
00:26:11.990 --> 00:26:16.180
You all get a move on too! You don't 
want to be late for the party!

361
00:26:18.280 --> 00:26:21.170
Our utopia is within our grasp.

362
00:26:29.990 --> 00:26:33.400
I will not abide further trouble.

363
00:26:33.870 --> 00:26:35.860
Please leave it to us, Boss!

364
00:26:36.690 --> 00:26:38.650
You can count on us!

365
00:26:39.730 --> 00:26:41.640
Go enjoy yourselves!

366
00:26:46.530 --> 00:26:49.670
I'm sorry for being 
so unseemly, Vivi-chan.

367
00:26:49.670 --> 00:26:51.570
No, nothing of the sort!

368
00:26:51.570 --> 00:26:53.610
Well, Uncle, we should be off!

369
00:26:53.610 --> 00:26:56.170
Oh, Luffy-kun. 
Take this with you.

370
00:26:56.740 --> 00:26:58.110
Wow! Water!

371
00:26:58.110 --> 00:26:59.320
Water!

372
00:26:59.320 --> 00:27:00.130
You found some?!

373
00:27:00.750 --> 00:27:05.020
Last night, just after you
fell asleep while digging,

374
00:27:05.020 --> 00:27:07.850
I reached a moist layer of sand.

375
00:27:08.480 --> 00:27:11.790
That water is the moisture
I managed to extract from it!

376
00:27:11.790 --> 00:27:14.820
Oh! That sounds 
pretty complicated, but thanks!

377
00:27:15.280 --> 00:27:20.320
It's genuine Yuba water!
I'm sorry it's all I could get.

378
00:27:20.880 --> 00:27:23.020
I'll drink it with care!

379
00:27:31.810 --> 00:27:34.210
Luffy! What're you doing?!

380
00:27:37.990 --> 00:27:39.130
Luffy?

381
00:27:39.670 --> 00:27:41.300
What's wrong, Luffy-san ?

382
00:27:46.430 --> 00:27:47.310
I quit.

383
00:27:48.500 --> 00:27:49.650
Huh?

384
00:27:51.230 --> 00:27:52.310
You "quit"?

385
00:27:52.760 --> 00:27:54.770
Luffy-san... What do you mean?

386
00:27:54.770 --> 00:27:56.600
C'mon, Luffy!

387
00:27:56.600 --> 00:28:01.370
We know you often act on a whim, 
but there's no time for this! Get up!

388
00:28:01.940 --> 00:28:03.160
Aren't we going back?

389
00:28:03.690 --> 00:28:04.910
That's right.

390
00:28:04.910 --> 00:28:08.910
Stopping the revolt means going to Katorea, 
which is back the way we came.

391
00:28:08.910 --> 00:28:14.000
A million citizens are gonna clash 
and make a mess of this country!

392
00:28:14.720 --> 00:28:17.530
This is for Vivi-chan! Now Let's go!

393
00:28:18.720 --> 00:28:20.260
That's boring.

394
00:28:21.130 --> 00:28:22.510
Say what?!

395
00:28:24.000 --> 00:28:24.510
Vivi!

396
00:28:25.100 --> 00:28:26.260
Yes?

397
00:28:27.200 --> 00:28:30.310
I wanna kick Crocodile's ass!

398
00:28:31.870 --> 00:28:35.970
If we stop the people rebelling,
will that stop Crocodile?

399
00:28:36.460 --> 00:28:39.780
Besides, it's not like we can 
really do much in Katorea.

400
00:28:40.760 --> 00:28:44.510
After all, we're pirates. Things are 
better off without us around.

401
00:28:45.990 --> 00:28:49.660
Even if he's a moron, 
he makes a good point.

402
00:28:50.090 --> 00:28:52.960
That's Luffy for you.

403
00:28:52.960 --> 00:28:54.580
T-That's–

404
00:28:54.580 --> 00:28:58.890
You want to prevent people 
from dying in this battle.

405
00:29:00.590 --> 00:29:04.300
None of the citizens... 
and none of us!

406
00:29:06.540 --> 00:29:11.430
Even when facing a warlord of the 
sea and a million people going wild,

407
00:29:12.160 --> 00:29:14.730
you hope everyone
 will stay safe and sound.

408
00:29:16.940 --> 00:29:18.720
Isn't that being naive?

409
00:29:22.840 --> 00:29:26.160
Hold on, Luffy! 
Cut Vivi some slack already!

410
00:29:26.160 --> 00:29:27.460
Wait, Nami-san.

411
00:29:27.460 --> 00:29:28.490
But...

412
00:29:29.740 --> 00:29:31.590
Is it so wrong to want such a thing?

413
00:29:32.110 --> 00:29:35.250
Have I erred, 
not wanting people to die?!

414
00:29:36.760 --> 00:29:38.380
People die.

415
00:29:42.680 --> 00:29:45.040
Don't give me that!

416
00:29:45.680 --> 00:29:47.630
Keep speaking and you'll pay!

417
00:29:49.180 --> 00:29:52.640
That's exactly what
we're trying to stop here!

418
00:29:53.440 --> 00:29:55.600
The Rebel Army, the Royal Army,

419
00:29:55.600 --> 00:29:58.480
and regular citizens 
have done nothing to deserve this!

420
00:29:59.150 --> 00:30:04.610
So why do people have to die...
when it's all Crocodile's fault?!

421
00:30:09.800 --> 00:30:13.910
Then why are you putting
your life on the line?!

422
00:30:14.580 --> 00:30:17.670
– Whoa, Luffy! You're going too far!
– Damn it, Luffy!

423
00:30:21.090 --> 00:30:25.270
Just one look at this kingdom
and even I can tell...

424
00:30:26.860 --> 00:30:27.850
Tell what?!

425
00:30:28.880 --> 00:30:31.260
...what most needs... to be done!

426
00:30:37.180 --> 00:30:40.980
Yuba, you see, can't be
beaten by some lousy sand!

427
00:30:41.940 --> 00:30:46.400
Do you think it's enough
to risk your life alone?

428
00:30:46.860 --> 00:30:50.450
Then what should I be risking?!

429
00:30:53.710 --> 00:30:56.790
I can't let him get away with this!

430
00:30:57.370 --> 00:30:58.250
I've got–

431
00:31:00.820 --> 00:31:05.090
I've got nothing else to give...

432
00:31:07.730 --> 00:31:10.890
Why don't you try risking
 all of our lives together!

433
00:31:11.300 --> 00:31:12.550
Aren't we crewmates?!

434
00:31:16.480 --> 00:31:18.010
Aren't we crewmates?

435
00:31:22.160 --> 00:31:26.480
So, you're able to cry 
those kinds of tears after all.

436
00:31:33.950 --> 00:31:36.790
We will stop the rebellion!

437
00:31:38.290 --> 00:31:41.920
I know you actually hate this
and want to beat him up the most!

438
00:31:56.340 --> 00:31:57.510
Now tell me...

439
00:32:00.510 --> 00:32:02.510
where Crocodile is!

